      "id": "p1",
      "text": "Warmer spring weather is making the dangerous trek less treacherous, leading to a monthly increase in apprehension figures along the U.S. border. Border agents doing their job caught over 8,200 people in March. While overall immigration statistics still show historically low crossing rates, the political deadlock in Congress means lawmakers can't agree on funding for the agencies everyone depends on, leaving the system stuck.",
